  "plan": "doc/design/tenant_resource_entitlement_plan.md",
  "implemented": [
    "Tenant and personal login permissions now come from the tenant authorization selection; no platform public resources, legacy package relation or persisted resource-mode branch is consulted in that path",
    "Only the selected tenant role namespace participates; platform permission resolution remains in the platform branch",
    "Tenant authorization selection validates local resource scope, hierarchy, lifecycle, entitlement, public entries and alias targets using bounded scalar queries",
    "Explicit baseline application membership can distribute non-grantable public executable entries such as My Items; unrelated public resources remain excluded",
    "Exclusive next entitlement transition is carried in AuthorizationContext and preserved across the actual RPC codec and application JSON mapper",
    "Cache validation enforces the exclusive deadline independently of invalidation revisions; TTL is bounded, subsecond results are not cached, expired provider results are re-evaluated once then rejected",
    "Authorization revision is captured before membership/owner/role reads so concurrent ownership transfer does not stamp old policy with the new revision",
    "Deleted tenants are explicitly excluded from personal resolution and cache revision queries"
  ],
